#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0405 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "PARAMCD is blank on every row. Every grouping key then carries a blank component, so every group is dropped under the shipped DROP_MISSING_KEYS default and nothing can fire; independently the per-row not empty(PARAMCD) conjunct is false everywhere. The rule EXECUTES and reports nothing although the ATOXDSCH values disagree. Keep PARAMCD declared -- only its values are blank; deleting the column would instead make var_exists(\"PARAMCD\") false and test a different thing."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col AVISITN  type=Num
col AVAL     type=Num
col ATOXDSCH type=Char
---
S1 | 001 |  | 1 | 5.0 | GRADE1
S1 | 001 |  | 2 | 5.1 | GRADE1
S1 | 001 |  | 3 | 5.2 | GRADE2
